# UI System

## Component Library

- Use shadcn/ui components whenever applicable.
- Reuse existing project components before creating new ones.
- Do not install another UI component library.
- Do not recreate components that already exist.

## Visual Consistency

- Follow the existing design system.
- Reuse existing spacing, typography, borders, radius, shadows, and sizing.
- Do not introduce arbitrary values when an existing design token can be used.
- Keep visual hierarchy consistent across pages.

## Layout

- Use responsive layouts.
- Design mobile-first.
- Maintain consistent page padding and content widths.
- Avoid unnecessary nested containers.

## Colors

- Use semantic theme variables.
- Do not hardcode colors unless explicitly required.
- Status colors must have consistent meaning:
  - outage
  - upcoming
  - active
  - resolved

## Typography

- Use the project's established font.
- Reuse existing text styles.
- Avoid excessive font-weight variation.

## Components

Before creating a component:

1. Search the existing components.
2. Check shadcn/ui.
3. Reuse or extend an existing component when possible.
4. Only create a new component when necessary.

## UX

- Loading states must exist for asynchronous content.
- Empty states must be intentional.
- Errors must be understandable to users.
- Interactive elements must have visible states.
- Maintain keyboard accessibility.

## Do Not

- Introduce random gradients.
- Add unnecessary animations.
- Add excessive rounded cards.
- Use inconsistent button styles.
- Create one-off UI patterns without justification.